# Checkpoint — zombie FPS (clean room, zombie-fps-local-ai)

## TASK
Build/verify the FPS in THIS folder per GAME_GOAL.md + AGENTS.md; when it genuinely works, write REPORT.md and STOP.
Immutable constraints:
- RULE ZERO: internal consistency is NOT evidence. Prove orientation from SCREEN-SPACE PROJECTION (ndc signs / projected screen coords), not from internal numbers agreeing.
- Clean room: never read/copy code from other projects (esp. old fps-grid-calibration). Three.js local only (./three.module.js), no CDN/external assets.
- Blocking defects (must have none): reversed W/S or A/D; movement not camera-relative after turning; crosshair not at exact viewport centre; crosshair-to-hit misalignment; zombie dying on 4th or surviving 5th valid hit; fatal page errors.
- Movement: W = camera forward projected on ground, S = opposite, A = strafe screen-left, D = strafe screen-right; pitch must not move player vertically.
- Aim: authoritative ray from camera centre (crosshair), NOT from gun barrel.
- Two zombies: A stationary, B walks slowly toward player (stops ~dist<=2.2). Both block-built humanoids, health bar over head, exactly 5 HP (5th valid hit kills, not 4th/6th), dead zombie no longer targetable.
- Evidence standard: mechanically verified vs visually inspected vs human-only must be separated in REPORT.md.

## CURRENT PRODUCT STATE
- Files: `index.html` (entry, viewport 1280x800), `game.js` (718 lines, whole game), `three.module.js` (vendored).
- Served at http://127.0.0.1:8802/ (curl 200 confirmed this session). Entry = index.html.
- IMPORTANT: `THREE` is NOT a page global (ES module import) — do NOT reference THREE in codex-browser eval.
- Hooks: window.__AGENT_STATE__ (player logical+world pos, camera yaw/pitch/forward, crosshair target, lastShot hit/miss+targetId, both zombies hp/world pos, ready, pointerLocked) and window.__THREE_GAME_TEST_HOOKS__ (fire, setYaw, setPitch, setPlayerPosition, setZombiePosition, resetZombieHp, respawn, setDebugLabels, setCalibrationTarget, projectToScreen, projectLogical, holdKey/releaseKey/releaseAllKeys, getCamera, getState).
- Coordinate convention (game.js top comment): logical (x,z) -> world (x,0,-z). Spawn (0,0), yaw=0 -> camera fwd world (0,0,-1) = logical +Y. Verified live this session: camera matrixWorld origin (0,1.7,0), dir (0,0,-1).
- Zombies: A logical (-2.5,11) stationary; B (2.5,11) walks toward player, stops at dist<=2.2. Both HP=5.
- Aim code (game.js): aimRay() = raycaster.setFromCamera(Vector2(0,0), camera); crosshairTarget() iterates zombieWorldHitboxes(z) and ray.intersectBox(box, target); fire() uses crosshairTarget(). intersectBox in three.module.js (line ~5709) is the standard slab test — reads correct.
- zombieWorldHitboxes (game.js ~L323): builds AABBs from per-mesh geometry bboxes offset by mesh.position, rotates by group rotation.y via rot(v) = (x*cy - z*sy, y, x*sy + z*cy), adds group.position. NOTE: geometry bboxes are centred on mesh origin; meshes with rotation.y (zombie arms ry=±0.08) get unrotated local bboxes — tiny error, NOT the cause.
- Runtime status: page loads, __AGENT_STATE__ updates (ready:true, time advancing, zombie B moving — B at (2.45,10.781) at t=0.25 proves loop runs).

## COMPLETED (mechanically verified via codex-browser eval)
1. Crosshair DOM center == viewport center (640,400) EXACT (getBoundingClientRect).
2. Screen-projection proof at spawn: (0,1) ndc z=0.900 in front, sx=640 sy=1061 (front); (0,-1) behind; diagonals (-1,1) ndc.x=-0.860 left-front, (1,1) +0.860 right-front, (-1,-1)/(1,-1) behind => W front, S back, A left, D right, all 8 combos correct.
3. Movement yaw=0: W (0,+4.299), S (0,-4.298), A (-4.298,0), D (+3.999,0).
4. Camera-relative: yaw=+90deg W (+4.099,0) A (0,+4.398) D (0,-4.199); yaw=-90deg W (-3.999,0) A (0,-4.1) D (0,+4.499).
5. Pitch 0.9 + W -> player y stays 1.7 (no vertical drift).
6. Calibration target logical (0,11) h=1.7 -> screen (640,400), ndc (0,0) at yaw=0 (crosshair<->ray agreement on centre line).
7. Fixed earlier: syncCamera() stale-quaternion bug (camera.rotation reset but not quaternion -> stale aim ray). Fixed via camera.quaternion.identity() (game.js ~line 162).
8. THIS SESSION: confirmed live ray after respawn + setZombiePosition('A',0,11) + yaw/pitch 0: origin (0,1.7,0), dir (0,0,-1) — exactly the centre ray. crosshair still null.

## UNRESOLVED
BLOCKING: crosshairTarget() returns null in EVERY tested aim — including zombie A placed directly on the centre line at logical (0,11) with yaw=0/pitch=0, where the torso box (world x=0, y=0.85..1.6, z=-11.17..-10.83) plainly contains the centre ray (ray passes through x=0,y=1.7 at z=-11 -> inside torso y-range). Manual slab math: t=11, inside all slabs -> MUST hit. Game reports no hit.
Suspects (in order):
(a) NEW this session: codex-browser eval'd setInterval step-drivers did NOT fire (window.__Tn.step stayed 0 after 1.5s) — either codex-browser eval runs in a different execution context than the page (so H.getState() etc. from eval may hit a DIFFERENT window/game instance than the one rendering!), or the page is frozen. NOTE: direct eval reads of __AGENT_STATE__ and getCamera() DID return live values consistent with the rendering loop, so same-context is likely; the interval failure is unexplained.
(b) zombieWorldHitboxes() box construction/rotation (game.js ~L323) — needs live dump of the actual Box3 min/max values.
(c) raycaster using stale camera matrix — ray origin/dir confirmed correct this session via matrixWorld, so aimRay origin/dir are fine; the MISS must be in the boxes or in intersectBox input.
Debug plan: dump from INSIDE the page (not eval): add a temporary module-level hook in game.js, e.g. window.__DBG = { boxes: () => zombies.map(z => ({id: z.id, pos: z.group.position.toArray(), rotY: z.group.rotation.y, boxes: zombieWorldHitboxes(z).map(b => ({min: b.min.toArray(), max: b.max.toArray()}))})), ray: () => { const rc = aimRay(); return {o: rc.ray.origin.toArray(), d: rc.ray.direction.toArray()}; }, test: () => crosshairTarget() }, then read via codex-browser eval. Compare box coords vs ray.

## LAST TEST
codex-browser eval: set up interval step-driver window.__Tn (respawn, place A at (0,11), read state after 80ms).
Result: after ~1.5s, window.__Tn.out = null, step = 0 — the setInterval callback never ran, so the post-placement state read never happened. (Earlier direct evals in the same session DID see live __AGENT_STATE__ and correct camera ray, so the page itself is alive.)

## NEXT INTENDED ACTION
Add a temporary in-module debug hook to game.js (window.__DBG with boxes()/ray()/test() as in UNRESOLVED(b)), reload the page, place zombie A at logical (0,11) via __THREE_GAME_TEST_HOOKS__ (respawn -> setZombiePosition -> wait 1 frame via a simple setTimeout-free trick: read __AGENT_STATE__ twice with a small sleep between codex-browser calls, since the loop re-syncs camera each frame), then read window.__DBG.boxes() and window.__DBG.ray() and compare by hand. Fix whatever mismatch is found (most likely: hitbox min/max vs ray). Then re-verify: aim A -> targetId 'A'; aim B -> 'B'; offset yaw -> near-miss null + fire() miss. Remove __DBG after fixing.

## SKILLS
Loaded (relevant): threejs-qa-release (test hooks __THREE_GAME_TEST_HOOKS__ / __AGENT_STATE__ convention, playtest-bot.md), threejs-debug-profiler (camera/input/transform debugging, scene-debugging checklist), threejs-gameplay-systems (FPS controls, camera-relative movement, raycast/hit detection, update order). threejs-game-ui-designer (crosshair/health bar), threejs-aaa-graphics-builder (block visuals), game-engine/game-developer (3d-web-games.md) available as needed. threejs-game-director not needed.

