## DO NOT REPEAT
- Do NOT accept internal consistency (HUD/labels/transform agreeing) as proof of orientation — must use screen-space projection (ndc signs / projected screen coords).
- Do NOT reference THREE in codex-browser eval (not a global).
- Do NOT read/copy code from other projects (clean room).
- codex-browser eval does NOT await Promises/async — (async()=>{...})() returns {}. Use setInterval step-driver pattern (window.__Tn={step,plan,timer}, advance ~80ms/step, then read window.__Tn.out) to wait between state changes.
- Camera re-syncs only on the next animation frame after setYaw/setPlayerPosition — always wait >=1 frame before reading __AGENT_STATE__ or firing.
- Arrow-function `this` inside setInterval callbacks bound via `.bind(window.__Tn)` did NOT work in codex-browser eval this session (step stayed 0). If step-drivers fail again, prefer: make the wait part of the GAME (e.g. a temporary in-module hook that captures values on the next frame) instead of eval-side timers.

